* sky130-gcedram -- access-device off-state leakage testbench
* Issue #2: retention/refresh budget evidence chain, link 1 of 3
* (device leakage -> storage-node capacitance assumption -> retention
* derivation in #3). See sim/leakage/README.md for the full writeup.
*
* Device under test: sky130_fd_pr__nfet_01v8 (sky130 core 1.8V NMOS),
* the candidate 2T/3T gain-cell access device -- see sim/leakage/README.md
* "Device choice" for the rationale. Geometry: W=0.42um L=0.15um, the
* minimum drawn size for this model (an explicit sizing ASSUMPTION,
* revisited by the retention derivation in #3, not a ratified spec value).
*
* Bias point (worst-case retention scenario -- access transistor holding
* off a storage node that was last written to a logic '1', unselected
* bitline sitting at ground):
*   gate (wl)            = 0 V   -- access transistor held OFF
*   drain (sn, storage)  = VDD   -- storage node holds a charged logic '1'
*   source (bl)          = 0 V   -- unselected bitline, maximizes Vds
*   body                 = 0 V   -- core NMOS, body tied to substrate/VSS
*
* Reports the DC current drawn from the storage-node source (vsn), which
* is the total off-state leakage discharging that node: BSIM4 subthreshold
* channel current plus the reverse-biased drain-body junction diode current
* (diomod=1 in the shipped model). Gate leakage is NOT captured -- the
* shipped sky130_fd_pr__nfet_01v8 model sets igcmod=igbmod=0 (no gate
* tunneling current model in this PDK release); this is a modeling-scope
* limitation, noted here, not folded into the reported number.
*
* Corner and temperature are substituted by
* sim/leakage/run_leakage_sweep.py -- @@CORNER@@ in {tt, ss, ff, sf, fs}
* (the sky130 MOS process corners shipped in
* libs.tech/combined/sky130.lib.spice) and @@TEMP_C@@ in {-40, 27, 125}
* (the temperature points named in the shipped
* libs.tech/irsim/*_{n40,27,125}.prm corner files, and the range the
* sky130-bandgap ratified spec uses for retention/temperature claims).
* Uses ONLY this .lib include from the shipped PDK -- no local model edits.

.param VDD = 1.8

.lib "@@PDK_NGSPICE_LIB@@" @@CORNER@@

.temp @@TEMP_C@@

xdut sn wl bl 0 sky130_fd_pr__nfet_01v8 l=0.15 w=0.42

vsn sn 0 dc {VDD}
vwl wl 0 dc 0
vbl bl 0 dc 0

.control
op
let ileak_a = abs(i(vsn))
print ileak_a
.endc

.end
